<spell-notebook "embed usage">
	<header level="1">
		Embed
		<header>An embed displays content from other websites, like YouTube videos, loaded only when asked
              for.</>
	</>
	<embed-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#using-it">Using it</>
			<item link="#privacy">Privacy</>
			<item link="#events">Events</>
			<item link="#behaviors">Behaviors</>
			<item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
			<item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
			<item link="#framework-usage">Framework usage</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  sources, privacy, events, script API, keyboard, accessibility, frameworks. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			Write `<ui-embed>` with what to show; there is no `.embed()` call to make. The content comes from:

			- `source` (`youtube` or `vimeo`) plus `video-id` (Fomantic's `data-id`: `id` is the element's own) -- your
			  backend stores the meaningful id, the element builds the URL
			- or any `http(s)` `url` (other protocols are refused); a YouTube / Vimeo URL gets their player parameters

			`placeholder` is the image shown before the frame loads, `icon` the icon over it (`icon="false"` for none),
			`label` names it (default `alt`, else "video" / "embedded content"). `autoplay` is on by default, since the
			click already asked for the video; `branded-ui` keeps the player's branding, and the `parameters` property adds
			URL parameters (`{ start: 30 }`).
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Privacy">
		<markdown>
			Until it's activated, an embed makes no request to the other site, not even a preconnect. Fomantic loaded the
			frame at once; here the placeholder is a real `<button>`, and only a click (or **Enter** / **Space**) loads the
			`<iframe>`. YouTube videos play from `youtube-nocookie.com`.
		</>
		<message size="small" class="site-not-ported">Not ported: custom sources (<text code>$.fn.embed.settings.sources</>), and Fomantic's per-source hd and color settings. Give any other player its <text code>url</>, and its options through <text code>parameters</>.</>
	</>

	<section label="Events">
		<markdown>
			- `ui-loading` -- about to load the frame from `url` (a click, **Enter** / **Space**, `host.activate()`);
			  `detail` is `{ url, originalEvent? }`. `preventDefault()` keeps the placeholder: the place to ask for
			  consent.
			- `ui-reset` -- back to the placeholder (`host.reset()`, Fomantic's `reset`); the frame is gone.

			Writing `active` loads the frame without an event.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```js
			const tour = document.querySelector("ui-embed")
			tour.parameters = { start: 30 }
			tour.addEventListener("ui-loading", (event) => {
			  if (!consent.video) {
			    event.preventDefault() // keep the placeholder
			    askForConsent()
			  }
			})
			tour.reset() // back to the placeholder
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Behaviors">
		<markdown>
			Fomantic's behaviors are methods and properties on the host:

			- `change(source, id, url)` -- set `source` / `video-id` / `url`
			- `reset` -- `host.reset()`
			- `show` -- `host.activate()` (fires `ui-loading`), or `host.active = true` (no event)
			- `get url`, `get id`, `get placeholder` ... -- read the attributes
			- `has placeholder` -- `host.placeholder`
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			- **Tab** reaches the play button.
			- **Enter** / **Space** loads the frame and moves focus into it.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- The placeholder is a real `<button>` named "Play" plus the `label` ("Play Fomantic UI intro"; translated).
			  Give every embed a `label`: it also becomes the frame's `title`, which is how screen readers name an
			  `<iframe>`.
			- Once activated, focus moves into the frame, so keyboard users land on the player they asked for.
			- The video's own controls and captions are the other site's.
			- If the element fails to render, the video is gone: no play button, no frame,
			  and no `ui-loading`, `reset()` or focus move.
			  Only children written inside the element still show, through a bare `<slot>`.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Framework usage">
		<markdown>Set `parameters` as a property, and listen for `ui-loading` to gate loading.</>
		<header level="4" id="framework-react">React 19</>
		<markdown>
			```jsx
			<ui-embed source="youtube" video-id={id} label={title} parameters={{ start: 30 }} onui-activate={track} />
			```
		</>
		<header level="4" id="framework-vue">Vue 3.5</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<!-- compilerOptions.isCustomElement = (tag) => tag.startsWith("ui-") -->
			<ui-embed source="youtube" :video-id="id" :label="title" :parameters="{ start: 30 }" @ui-loading="track" />
			```
		</>
		<header level="4" id="framework-solid">Solid 2</>
		<markdown>
			```jsx
			// events and rich data are plain props:  `on-<event>={...}`, `options={...}`
			<ui-embed
			  source="youtube"
			  video-id={id}
			  label={title}
			  parameters={{ start: 30 }}
			  on-ui-loading={track}
			/>
			```
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
